.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt ULIMIT 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ulimit
.Nd POSIX resource-limit command surface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl HS
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl cdfnstv
.Op Ar limit
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads and writes the calling process's soft and hard resource limits
through the kernel
.Fn proc_getrlimit
and
.Fn proc_setrlimit
calls.
.Pp
The
.Fl a
form reports every resource. File and core sizes are shown in 512-byte
blocks, data/stack/address space in kbytes, and CPU time in seconds; the
value
.Dq unlimited
maps to the infinite limit. The
.Fl H
and
.Fl S
options select the hard or soft limit (the soft limit is the default).
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success; a usage error exits with status 2 and a rejected limit
with status 1.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1
